From d9414644331caec38402cdc7927d17f75d62e75a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Midgy BALON <midgy971@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 11:11:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] sunxi: A523: read the U-Boot FIT from the configured raw
 sector

board_spl_mmc_get_uboot_raw_sector() computed sector = max(raw_sect,
spl_size/512), but sunxi_get_spl_size() returns a bogus value on the A523,
yielding sector ~0xe000 (28 MiB) instead of the configured location. The SPL
then read garbage instead of the FIT, found no image, and jumped to an empty
load address (silent hang). Return the configured
CONFIG_SYS_MMCSD_RAW_MODE_U_BOOT_SECTOR directly; it is deterministic for the
128 KiB SD boot layout (SPL @128K, FIT @256K).

Assisted-by: Claude (Opus 4.8)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/board.c b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/board.c
index 301ac2c4619..2f1e49091af 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/board.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/board.c
@@ -356,7 +356,7 @@ unsigned long board_spl_mmc_get_uboot_raw_sector(struct mmc *mmc,
 	unsigned long spl_size = sunxi_get_spl_size();
 	unsigned long sector;
 
-	sector = max(raw_sect, spl_size / 512);
+	sector = raw_sect; (void)spl_size; /* FIT at fixed RAW_MODE sector */
 	return sector; /* A523 deterministic 128K boot */
 
 	switch (sunxi_get_boot_source()) {
